<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Print on demand</h2>
<p>Before launching print on demand automation, prove every app in the stack logs email and SMS consent auditably, with purchase events cutting promotional follow-up the moment checkout completes. Print On Demand audiences forgive plain creative; they do not forgive promos sent mid-refund or right after checkout.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>No print on demand promos without proof; transactional messages only</td><td>Without print on demand consent proof, marketing has no legal footing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Open print on demand with guidance and proof, not discounts</td><td>Premature print on demand offers teach shoppers to wait</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Print On Demand reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Margin-safe print on demand recovery at peak intent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Print On Demand buyers get education, not another pitch</td><td>Keeps print on demand buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Print On Demand selling waits for case resolution</td><td>Service-active print on demand shoppers reject promos</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Sunset cold print on demand contacts before complaints build</td><td>Keeps print on demand placement high via list hygiene</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold print on demand texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>One print on demand SMS complaint outweighs many email ones</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Print On Demand wholesale accounts get dedicated messaging</td><td>Wholesale print on demand terms forbid retail-style offers</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Verify print on demand throwaway addresses pre-journey</td><td>Print On Demand list quality decides placement</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Keep print on demand staff and test profiles out of live sends</td><td>Internal print on demand activity corrupts program metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>No bespoke print on demand track for competitor signals</td><td>Print On Demand one-offs breed audit gaps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Reconfirm print on demand consent where timestamps are missing</td><td>Timestamp-less print on demand consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Print on demand</h2>
<p>For print on demand, revenue attribution flatters; margin decides. Burden the print on demand program with its true load — platform fees, overages, SMS, capture, creative, agency, and print on demand discount cost — before calling it profitable. If print on demand tooling eats toward fifteen percent of attributed margin, reduce print on demand scope before optimizing flows.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. Before banking on free for print on demand, check which free-tier limit — contacts, sends, branching, support — hits your print on demand plan earliest.</p>
